- TOCTOU between mint and apply: tokens map stores a JSON-cloned (deep-copy)
  candidate at mint time; apply re-runs the same helper on that same
  immutable value. No path for a non-current candidate to reach apply with
  nil/disabled rules once gated at mint (missing-policy/failed rejection
  modes in TestSpendingApplyRejections still 409 as before).
- Baseline vs Kind/staleness: loadSpendingSnapshot's revision+fingerprint+
  scenario check runs unconditionally in the apply handler regardless of
  Kind, so a stale "current" token still 409s on any settings edit
  (TestSpendingApplyRejections "revision"/"fingerprint"/"scenario" modes
  unchanged and still passing).

No reproducible defect found within CP1's stated scope.
